  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HMIS in low resource settings</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for national health information systems, with focus on core software, capacity building, action research and strengthening goveranance.

The following countries are using HMIS as national health information systems: Afghanistan, Algeria, Angola, Bangladesh, Benin, Bhutan, Botswana, Burkina Faso, Burundi, Cameroon, Cape Verde, Chad, Comoros, Dem. Rep. Congo, Djibouti, East Timor, Eritrea, Ethiopia, Ghana, Guinea, Guinea Bissau, Haiti, Honduras, Indonesia, Ivory Coast, Kenya, Kyrgyzstan, Laos, Lebanon, Lesotho, Liberia, Libya, Madagascar, Malawi, Maldives, Mali, Mauritania, Mauritius, Morocco, Mozambique, Myanmar, Namibia, Nepal, Niger, Nigeria and Pakistan.</narrative>
  </description>
